.TH COOLER-BTOP 1 "2026-09-13" "cooler-btop 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cooler-btop \- monitor Linux system resources in a terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cooler-btop
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cooler-btop
shows CPU, memory, storage, network, GPU, IPv4 TCP listening-port, and process telemetry in a Textual terminal interface.
The web server is started only when
.B \-\-daemon
or
.B \-\-serve
is supplied.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-desktop
Use application-menu error handling. If startup fails in an interactive
terminal, display the error and wait for Enter before closing the window.
.TP
.BR \-\-daemon , " " \-\-serve
Run the local web dashboard and metrics API instead of the terminal interface.
.TP
.BR \-\-host " " HOST
Set the web server bind address. The default is 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.BR \-\-port " " PORT
Set the web server port. The default is 8080.
.TP
.BR \-\-log-db " " PATH
Write daemon metrics to the specified SQLite database.
.TP
.BR \-\-interval " " SECONDS
Set the telemetry update interval. The default is 1.0 second.
.TP
.B \-\-no-pet
Disable the animated terminal pet.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Query the local daemon and print a short status report.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the installed version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command-line help and exit.
.SH FILES
The application does not create a system service or start a background daemon during installation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ps (1),
.BR top (1)
